Spec: server

Purpose:
  Own the whole HTTP surface and transport posture of the diagnostic server: the three-GET-route
    axum @Router built by @create_router; @instance_handler's fixed pipeline that answers
    shape, kind, item and dot-lane rejections before any identity is touched, then
    authenticates (./auth.rs), authorizes (./authz.rs), gates instance existence and dispatches
    to ./collect/; @run_server's listener choice — plain HTTP, plain TLS, or the mandatory
    client-cert-mTLS that makes `--trust-request-header` safe, with the startup refusal of the
    trust flag without TLS; the `application/yaml` labelling of YAML bodies; and the
    `X-Diag-Redactions` scrub tally injected into every response a redacting collector produced.
    This file is the crate's security boundary for transport: nothing in ./auth.sdd binds a
    parsed header to a verified channel — that guarantee exists only in the TLS code here.

Owns:
  ./server.rs

References:
  ./error.sdd — the @DiagError vocabulary every `?` here feeds; the per-variant `DIAG-` id,
    status and JSON `{code,message}` @IntoResponse rendering every failure leg below names.
  ./auth.sdd — the @extract_identity decision this file places in the pipeline and feeds with
    cloned headers; its trust-boundary `[?]` and the flag's `--trust-request-header` flag/env
    pair from ./config.sdd own the header-trust semantics, the TLS binding here does not.
  ./authz.sdd — @check_item_access and @is_instance_scoped_item consumed once each; item
    membership pre-validation exists because @check_item_access default-allows unknown items.
  ./config.sdd — the @Config fields @run_server and the handler read; parse-time validation
    boundaries (empty `bind` accepted, missing TLS files not detected).
  ./state.sdd — the @AppState cloned into the router and re-read per request; the ./main.rs
    `ring` provider pin this file's plain-TLS listener depends on.
  ./dto.sdd — @ScrubStats, whose @distinct and @occurrences @usize fields the
    `X-Diag-Redactions` grammar hardcodes.
  ./discovery.sdd — @discovery_handler as mounted here unauthenticated; the duplicated
    @API_GROUP and @API_VERSION constants and the unauthenticated-discovery exemption are
    `[?]` there.
  ./collect/clusterinfo.sdd, ./collect/vynilconfig.sdd, ./collect/packages.sdd,
    ./collect/popularity_contest.sdd, ./collect/state.sdd, ./collect/children.sdd,
    ./collect/logs.sdd — the collectors each dispatch arm awaits, including who returns
    @ScrubStats and who returns plain @String bodies (./collect/logs.sdd: all three are
    (@String, @ScrubStats) pairs).
  ./common/src/instancetenant.sdd, ./common/src/instanceservice.sdd,
    ./common/src/instancesystem.sdd — the typed gets @check_instance_exists needs installed.
  /server/src/error.sdd, /common/src/context.sdd — approved calibration references.

Must:
  @create_router registers exactly the three GET routes @API_PATH and @INSTANCE_PATH spell and
    nothing else — no fallback, no middleware layer, no nest or merge — so on
    this one @Router matched paths answer `200` (item lanes), unmatched paths the bare `404`
    axum 0.8.9 produces, matched paths other methods `405` (@StatusCode::METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED per
    axum 0.8.9), and trailing-slash variants miss their routes: `GET /healthz` →
    @healthz_handler, `GET /apis/admin.vynil.solidite.fr/v1` → @discovery_handler,
    `GET /apis/admin.vynil.solidite.fr/v1/namespaces/{ns}/{kind}/{name}/{item}` →
    @instance_handler, all closed over the cloned @AppState by @with_state.
  @VALID_KINDS is the literal @str array [`tenantinstances`, `serviceinstances`,
    `systeminstances`] and @VALID_ITEMS the nine-item array [`clusterinfo`, `vynilconfig`,
    `packages`, `popularitycontest`, `state`, `children`, `agentlog`, `childlogs`,
    `operatorlog`]; membership is an exact, whole-value, case-sensitive @contains of the
    percent-decoded params on @as_str — no trim, no case fold, no partial match.
  @DNS_1123_RE is the literal `^[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9.]*[a-z0-9])?$` (regex `1.12.4` @Regex behind a
    std @LazyLock) and @validate_dns1123 applies it to the `{ns}` and `{name}` params only, as
    an anchored full match: a leading or trailing `.` or `-` and the bare two-byte `..` are
    rejected, embedded dot runs — `a..b` — pass, a single alphanumeric passes. `{kind}` and
    `{item}` never face the regex, only the two allow-lists above.
  @instance_handler runs, first error short-circuiting via `?`: @validate_dns1123 on ns then on
    name (`@DiagError::InvalidNameFormat`, `400` `DIAG-003`) → @VALID_KINDS membership
    (`@DiagError::UnknownKind`, `404` `DIAG-004`) → @VALID_ITEMS membership
    (`@DiagError::UnknownItem`, `404` `DIAG-005`) → @extract_identity(client, headers,
    @state.config.trust_request_header) (`401` `DIAG-006` leg) →
    @check_item_access(client, identity, kind, ns, name, item, @state.config.enable_packages)
    (SAR refusal `403` `DIAG-001`, gated items `404` `DIAG-007`) → the existence gate, firing
    only when @is_instance_scoped_item(&item) and reached only after authz passed: @false from
    @check_instance_exists is @DiagError::InstanceNotFound (`404` `DIAG-002`) → the nine-arm
    @match on item. Shape, kind and item lanes therefore answer before any identity, before any
    cluster call and with no log line; the in-file comment gives the ordering rationale that
    authentication precedes cluster reads so the caller cannot probe instance existence
    unauthenticated — every read that touches the cluster with the server's own rights sits at
    or after @check_item_access.
  @check_instance_exists maps typed existence by @kind arm onto
    @common::instancetenant::@TenantInstance, @common::instanceservice::@ServiceInstance and
    @common::instancesystem::@SystemInstance through @kube::@Api::@namespaced(client, ns) and its
    @get: any @Ok answers @true, any @Err answers @false with the @kube::@Error discarded and
    unlogged, so absent, RBAC-denied and cluster-unreachable existence reads are one
    `404` `DIAG-002` lane; the `_` arm is unreachable behind the @VALID_KINDS pre-check.
  Generic-tier items never probe existence and never read the SAR lane (./authz.sdd tiering):
    `clusterinfo` serves regardless of path ns/name (which are never consulted by
    @get_cluster_info), `vynilconfig` serves the caller's `{ns}` into @get_vynil_config, and
    `packages`/`popularitycontest` answer for any authenticated identity while
    @state.config.enable_packages holds.
  Dispatch success envelopes on the locked axum `0.8.9`: every success is `200`; @axum::Json
    arms — `clusterinfo`, `packages`, `popularitycontest` (`@Json(...)` tuples) and `children`
    (@Json of @Vec<@ChildWithState> then @into_response) — carry `application/json`;
    `vynilconfig` and `state` go through @yaml_response and carry exactly
    `application/yaml` (CONTENT_TYPE inserted, no `charset` suffix); `agentlog`, `childlogs` and
    `operatorlog` hand the collectors' @String to axum @into_response and carry
    `text/plain; charset=utf-8`. @add_scrub_header runs on those six redacting arms — `state`,
    `children`, `vynilconfig`, `agentlog`, `childlogs`, `operatorlog` — via
    @response.headers_mut() after the body became a @Response (@insert, replacing any existing
    value), never on `clusterinfo`, `packages` or `popularitycontest`.
  @add_scrub_header builds the literal `distinct={distinct};occurrences={occurrences}`
    interpolated from @ScrubStats' decimal @usize fields under header name
    `X-Diag-Redactions`, and silently omits the header when @from_str refuses the value; digits
    and visible-ASCII grammar mean that omission is unreachable, but it errors into silence,
    not into a 500.
  @healthz_handler answers `(StatusCode::OK, "ok")` — `200`, body exactly `ok`, no extractor,
    no auth, and it is the only unauthenticated non-discovery route.
  @run_server runs this sequence in this order, every failure @DiagError and the binary's exit-1
    handling owned by ./main.rs: build the @Router with @create_router from a cloned state →
    parse @config.bind into @std::net::@SocketAddr via @str::@parse, payload
    `Invalid bind address: {e}` → guardrail: the combination of @config.trust_request_header with
    @config.insecure_no_tls is refused at startup with payload `DIAG-CONFIG: --trust-request-header requires TLS (mandatory mTLS). Refusing to start in an impersonable configuration.` →
    @config.insecure_no_tls branch: @tracing::warn! with `Starting HTTP server (no TLS) on {addr} — Bearer/TokenReview auth only`, then @axum::@serve on one @tokio::net::@TcpListener::@bind
    (addr) with payloads `HTTP bind error: {e}` and `HTTP server error: {e}`, returning @Ok when
    @serve finishes → TLS pair presence: @config.tls_cert and @config.tls_key both @Some else
    payload `TLS certificates not provided for HTTPS server` → @config.trust_request_header
    branch: @load_requestheader_ca then @build_mtls_config under the @tracing::info! line
    `Starting HTTPS server with MANDATORY mTLS (front-proxy CA self-loaded)` (that info line
    names no addr, unlike the plain-TLS one) → else
    @axum_server::tls_rustls::@RustlsConfig::from_pem_file on the two paths with payload
    `TLS config error: {e}` under the @tracing::info! line
    `Starting HTTPS server (server-side TLS) on {addr}` → finally @axum_server::@bind_rustls on
    the address and config, then its @serve of @into_make_service, with payload
    `HTTPS server error: {e}`. In
    the TLS paths @serve never returns in normal operation, so @Ok(()) is only ever observed
    after the listener stops.
  The trust flag is a single @bool read twice on this boundary — once at startup
    (@run_server: `true` with TLS builds the mTLS listener, `true` combined with no-TLS is
    refused) and
    once per request (@instance_handler hands it to @extract_identity) — no per-request
    transport fact reaches @instance_handler at all, and the file itself never reads
    `X-Remote-*` beyond the verbatim clone @RequestHeaders performs.
  @build_mtls_config: server cert chain via @rustls_pemfile::@certs and @rustls_pemfile::@private_key
    from the two @File paths (a @None key yields payload `no private key in key file`, file and
    PEM failures surface as @std::io::@Error or rustls text); the CA PEM @str is streamed through
    @rustls_pemfile::@cert and every certificate goes through @RootCertStore::@add; a
    @rustls::server::@WebPkiClientVerifier is @build from those roots on an explicit @Arc of
    @rustls::crypto::ring's @default_provider — the same provider ./main.rs installed globally,
    re-pinned locally — and
    installed via @with_client_cert_verifier, which on rustls `0.23.41` rejects handshakes
    without a client certificate chained to those roots, so reaching the application on this
    listener proves the front-proxy spoke with a certificate @load_requestheader_ca supplied;
    @with_safe_default_protocol_versions keeps rustls' own default versions; @ServerConfig is
    wrapped by @RustlsConfig::from_config in an @Arc. Every failure carries the payload prefix
    `mTLS config: `.
  @load_requestheader_ca prefers the override and is the only cluster reader in the startup
    path: @config.requestheader_ca @Some → @std::fs::@read_to_string verbatim, IO failure
    payload `requestheader CA file: {e}`; else one @get, through a namespaced
    @kube::@Api<@k8s_openapi::api::core::v1::@ConfigMap>, of
    `extension-apiserver-authentication` in `kube-system` (the
    `extension-apiserver-authentication-reader` RBAC grant is a deployment fact, not code here);
    a get failure is @map_err-d to @DiagError::KubeError — the only origin of that variant in
    this file — and a reply lacking the
    `requestheader-client-ca-file` key yields @DiagError::InternalError with payload
    `requestheader-client-ca-file absent de extension-apiserver-authentication`.
  @RequestHeaders is the file's only @FromRequestParts impl: its @from_request_parts clones
    @parts.headers wholesale, @Ok-ing unconditionally, so its @type Rejection @DiagError is
    declared but never produced and no header leg here can reject before the handler body.

Depends on:
  @crate::error::@DiagError — ./error.sdd: the only error type the router handlers yield; the
    @Debug and @thiserror derives plus @DiagError's @axum::response::IntoResponse impl are what let
    @instance_handler return `@Result<@Response, @DiagError>`; the derived @From conversions
    carry the collectors' `?` legs; @DiagError::KubeError enters only from the @ConfigMap leg.
  @crate::auth::@extract_identity (./auth.sdd), @crate::authz::@check_item_access and
    @crate::authz::@is_instance_scoped_item (./authz.sdd) — the auth and authz calls of the
    pipeline; @crate::discovery::@discovery_handler (./discovery.sdd) the mounted discovery
    body; @crate::config::@Config and @crate::state::@AppState (./config.sdd, ./state.sdd).
  ./collect/: @crate::collect::clusterinfo::@get_cluster_info, @vynilconfig::@get_vynil_config,
    @packages::@get_packages, @popularity_contest::@get_popularity_contest,
    @state::@get_instance_state, @children::@get_children, @logs::@get_agent_log,
    @logs::@get_child_logs, @logs::@get_operator_log — one per dispatch arm, payload and
    @ScrubStats ownership belongs to each sibling spec.
  @crate::dto::@ScrubStats (./dto.sdd) — the header tally's field names are coupled to it.
  @common::instancetenant::@TenantInstance, @common::instanceservice::@ServiceInstance,
    @common::instancesystem::@SystemInstance via /common/src/lib.rs — the typed existence gets;
    those CRDs must exist in the cluster for @Ok(true) ever.
  axum `0.8.9` locked in /Cargo.lock (`0.8` in /server/Cargo.toml): @Router, @get, @route,
    @with_state, @axum::extract::@Path, @State and @FromRequestParts, @axum::http::@StatusCode,
    @HeaderMap, @HeaderValue and @header::@CONTENT_TYPE, @axum::Json and @String's @IntoResponse
    lanes; the `404`/`405` defaults, automatic percent-decoding and per-param UTF-8 checks of
    @Path are that build's behavior, since no custom rejection or fallback overrides them here.
  axum-server `0.7.3` (`tls-rustls` feature): @RustlsConfig::from_pem_file and @from_config, plus
    @bind_rustls; the bind happens inside the @serve future (0.7.3 binds via @TcpListener there),
    and @from_pem_file builds its @rustls::@ServerConfig on the process default provider the
    ./main.rs `ring` pin supplied — @ring is passed explicitly only in @build_mtls_config.
  rustls `0.23.41` with the `ring` feature, rustls-pemfile `2.2.0` — verifier, roots, builder.
  kube `3.1.0` (@Client, @Api, @Api::@get) and k8s-openapi `0.27.1` (@ConfigMap) — CA load and
    existence gets only.
  regex `1.12.4` (@Regex::@new and @is_match), std @LazyLock, tokio `1.52.3` @TcpListener,
    @std::fs, @std::net — startup plumbing.
  @tracing `0.1` — the @warn! and @info! startup lines quoted in Must (the file logs nothing
    else).

Exposes:
  @create_router — `pub fn(@AppState) -> @Router`: the exact three-route table, GET-only,
    spelled in Must and Example; the sole registration site of every endpoint; no in-crate
    caller outside @run_server.
  @run_server — `pub async fn(@AppState, @Config) -> @Result<(), @DiagError>`: the binary's
    listener bootstrap consumed by ./main.rs, with the startup ladder and guardrail spelled out
    in Must; the
    doc comment names @DiagError::InternalError as the failure but a ConfigMap get failure
    leaves as @DiagError::KubeError and TLS/mTLS/CA-file/bind/guardrail payloads as
    @DiagError::InternalError — `500` `DIAG-500` renderings none of which reach a client because
    no listener is up yet.
  @RequestHeaders — `#[derive(@Debug)] pub struct(@pub @HeaderMap)` plus its
    @FromRequestParts impl (@type Rejection @DiagError, never produced): the crate-wide
    whole-request-header extractor, consumed so far only by @instance_handler, used nowhere
    else, and `pub` through `pub mod server;` in ./lib.rs.
  @API_GROUP — `pub const @API_GROUP: &@str =` `admin.vynil.solidite.fr`; @API_VERSION —
    `pub const @API_VERSION: &@str =` `v1`; duplicates of ./discovery.rs' same-named consts
    (there `[?]`'d) that neither file re-uses: the route literals repeat both strings inline.
  Private but observable on the wire, frozen at their own entries: the @API_PATH literal
    `/apis/admin.vynil.solidite.fr/v1` and @INSTANCE_PATH literal
    `/apis/admin.vynil.solidite.fr/v1/namespaces/{ns}/{kind}/{name}/{item}`; @VALID_KINDS and
    @VALID_ITEMS; @DNS_1123_RE and @validate_dns1123; @healthz_handler, @instance_handler,
    @check_instance_exists, @yaml_response, @add_scrub_header, @load_requestheader_ca,
    @build_mtls_config.

Accepts:
  @create_router: one @AppState by value, cloned in; the accepted request shapes per route:
    `GET /healthz` and `GET /apis/admin.vynil.solidite.fr/v1` take no body, no param, no header
    and no credential; `GET {INSTANCE_PATH}` accepts any four percent-decoding, UTF-8 path
    segments for `{ns}`, `{kind}`, `{name}`, `{item}` — arbitrary dot runs, `+`, other visible
    punctuation included (a non-UTF-8 or bad-escape param dies in @Path's default axum-0.8.9
    rejection, a bare `400` outside the @DiagError lane) — and headers, of which only the ones
    ./auth.sdd reads matter downstream. No body is ever read; @run_server accepts the resolved
    @Config read-only: `bind` gets its only shape check here, and TLS/CA paths are opened only
    by their branch, existence never probed first (./config.sdd).

Returns:
  @create_router: the @Router described; @run_server: @Ok(()) when the @serve future has
    returned — plain-HTTP mode ends only on a @serve error in practice, TLS modes not at all in
    normal operation; no other value.
  A wire table per lane: `200` on all successes (body/content-type per Dispatch Must; six arms
    additionally carry `X-Diag-Redactions: distinct={distinct};occurrences={occurrences}`);
    `400` `DIAG-003` ns/name regex, first failing param wins, name never tested when ns failed;
    `404` `DIAG-004` off-list kind; `404` `DIAG-005` off-list item; `401` `DIAG-006` every
    ./auth.sdd failure; `403` `DIAG-001` SAR denial; `404` `DIAG-007` gated item under the
    disabled flag; `404` `DIAG-002` gated-item existence @false; `500` `DIAG-500` for collector,
    SAR-post, kube and @DiagError::InternalError legs, all rendered as the JSON
    `{code,message}` ./error.sdd pins. `405` (bare) on a matched path's wrong method, `404` on
    unmatched paths, `400` from @Path rejections — axum 0.8.9 defaults, no `DIAG-` body. Startup
    lane payloads — `Invalid bind address:`, the guardrail `DIAG-CONFIG:` text, `HTTP bind error:`,
    `HTTP server error:`, `TLS certificates not provided`, `TLS config error:`,
    the `mTLS config: ` prefix, `requestheader CA file:`,
    `requestheader-client-ca-file absent`, and the @ConfigMap get's @DiagError::KubeError —
    never render to a client and go to ./main.rs's `error!` line and exit code `1`.

Raises:
  From this file's own code: @DiagError::InvalidNameFormat and @DiagError::UnknownKind from the
    shape and membership legs, @DiagError::UnknownItem, @DiagError::InstanceNotFound,
    @DiagError::InternalError at the bind, guardrail, insecure and TLS bootstrap legs listed in
    Must, @DiagError::KubeError at the @ConfigMap get. It forwards, untouched, whatever
    @extract_identity and @check_item_access raise. Collectors' errors propagate through `?`
    unaltered.
  @instance_handler is total: every leg answers @Ok or @Err, no @unwrap outside the @DNS_1123_RE
    build and no @panic anywhere reachable — the one @panic is the @unwrap_or_else arm for an
    invalid static pattern, impossible for the committed literal. @run_server raises before
    serving and blocks while serving; nothing in this file retries, times out, rate-limits or
    shuts listeners down gracefully.

Handles:
  All four `{@trust_request_header, @insecure_no_tls}` startup combinations: `true`+`false` →
    mandatory client-cert mTLS; `false`+`true` → plain HTTP with the warn line (mode note in
    Tasks `[?]`); `false`+`false` → plain server-side TLS; `true`+`true` → refused startup, the
    only combination with no listener.
  A `&&`-short-circuiting guardrail ordered after @SocketAddr parsing and router construction
    — with an unparsable bind plus the refused pair, the client-visible-elsewhere refusal loses
    to `Invalid bind address`, and neither is ever rendered until ./main.rs logs it.
  A partially supplied TLS pair (either @Some, @None) is refused by one message naming neither
    missing member.
  Path traversal input, stated frozen: `{ns}`/`{name}` reject leading/trailing `.` and the bare
    `..` at `400` (pre-auth, no cluster touch) and pass embedded dot runs `a..b` to
    @kube::@Api::@namespaced and its @get unaltered — gated items collapse any such collect or
    existence failure into `404` `DIAG-002`, ungated ones into a `500` kube lane; `{kind}` and
    `{item}` reject dots only incidentally — `..` and `.` answer `404` `DIAG-004`/`DIAG-005`
    because they match no list entry, pre-auth; this file performs no traversal-specific
    normalization beyond that.
  Percent-encodings decode before the checks (`%2e%2e` reaches the same lanes as `..`), while a
    bad escape or non-UTF-8 param dies at `400` in @Path, outside the @DiagError rendering.
  Existence-check failures at @instance_handler: `state`, `children`, `agentlog`, `childlogs`,
    `operatorlog` gate on it; the four generic/gated arms never probe it, so nonsense-but-valid
    ns/name combinations still serve cluster-wide or ns-scoped data on those arms.
  Scrub tally absence on the three non-redacting arms; @insert replacing a pre-existing
    `X-Diag-Redactions` value; the unreachable @from_str failure lane silently.
  Header-clone posture: @RequestHeaders copies the entire @HeaderMap — bearer tokens and
    `X-Remote-*` alike — into handler scope although @extract_identity, per ./auth.sdd, reads
    just three header names out of it.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover @create_router with in-memory @oneshot: 200 `ok` on `GET /healthz`; the fixed
      discovery body on the base path; `405` for non-GET on each registered path; bare `404` on
      unmatched and on trailing-slash variants.
  [ ] Cover the pipeline ordering with @tower on a @Router: off-shape ns (`..`, leading `-`)
      `400` before any auth; `..` kind and `..` item answered `404` `DIAG-004`/`DIAG-005`
      without credentials; `a..b` ns passing the regex and landing in the post-auth lanes;
      non-UTF-8 and bad-escape params taking the bare-`400` @Path lane, not `DIAG-003`.
  [ ] Cover the nine dispatch arms and header matrix (content types, `200`s, presence/absence of
      `X-Diag-Redactions`) with fake collectors or a fake apiserver; /server/Cargo.toml
      @dev-dependencies is empty and no httpmock/tower-test harness ships — the same missing
      harness ./auth.sdd and ./authz.sdd `[ ]` legs report.
  [ ] Cover @add_scrub_header grammar and @insert replacement, @yaml_response's
      `application/yaml` @CONTENT_TYPE.
  [ ] Cover @run_server startup refusals via @Config::try_parse_from-shaped test Configs: the
      `DIAG-CONFIG:` guardrail payload on trust+insecure (with a bind that parses, else the bind
      error wins — pin both orders), `Invalid bind address:` on garbage and on empty `bind`, the
      partial-pair TLS payload, and the warn line on insecure-only (loopback @SocketAddr +
      immediate connect, or assert before bind).
  [ ] Cover @build_mtls_config and @load_requestheader_ca with temp files: unreadable cert, PEM
      without key → `mTLS config: no private key in key file`, CA override reading verbatim; a
      rustls-level @ClientConfig handshake test could pin verifier refusal of
      certificate-less clients once rustls test tooling is agreed.
  [ ] Cover @check_instance_exists against fake-apiserver present/absent/denied replies — the
      present leg answers @true, denied and unreachable lanes still need the harness.
  [?] Existence error collapse: @check_instance_exists discards every @kube::@Error as @false,
      so RBAC gaps on the server's own instance reads and cluster outages answer
      `404` `DIAG-002` (false, not absent). Decide later whether existence `Err` should become
      `500`/`DIAG-500`.
  [?] Existence-blind generic arms: `clusterinfo` with an arbitrary valid ns and
      `vynilconfig` reading the caller's `{ns}` both answer after an authenticated-but
      possibly-empty identity; authz.sdd's pass-through posture is `[?]`'d there but this
      endpoint shape freezes whether it should keep accepting. Decide later after ./authz.sdd
      `[?]`.
  [?] Trust-flag coupling: `X-Remote-User` is trusted iff the process-wide flag is `true`, made
      safe by exactly one startup decision — @run_server checks the trust+insecure pair once,
      @instance_handler re-reads @state.config.trust_request_header per request, and no code
      rebinds a listener today, but a config mutated at runtime would open the header lane
      without any @Router rebuild. Decide later whether the lane should re-prove the startup
      pairing.
  [?] Guardrail payload `DIAG-CONFIG:` — the refusal payload begins `DIAG-CONFIG:`, an id
      format none of the eleven ./error.sdd variants produces, so a second pseudo-id rides
      inside the `500` `DIAG-500` @Display, alongside the mixed-French CA text
      `requestheader-client-ca-file absent de extension-apiserver-authentication` which today
      reaches only ./main.rs's log but is shaped like wire text. Decide later whether both
      strings are normalized, localized or kept.
  [?] Guardrail ordering: the trust+insecure check runs after @SocketAddr parsing and after
      @create_router, so a typo'd bind masks the security refusal (and a refused config builds
      a discarded router). Decide later whether it should become the first check.
  [?] Doc comment vs reality on @run_server: the `# Errors` doc names @DiagError::InternalError
      as the failure, but the ConfigMap get leg yields @DiagError::KubeError. Decide later
      whether the startup lane normalizes onto @DiagError::InternalError or the doc broadens to
      name both.
  [?] Dead/never lanes kept for defense: the `_` arms of @check_instance_exists and the
      @instance_handler @match are unreachable behind the allow-lists; @RequestHeaders'
      @Rejection is never produced; @API_GROUP and @API_VERSION are `pub` but unread crate-wide
      (./discovery.sdd `[?]` names the duplication). Decide later whether these get cfg'd away,
      folded into shared consts or stay.
  [?] @RequestHeaders clones every request header — credentials and front-proxy headers
      included — though nothing but @extract_identity reads them; @Debug on the struct makes the
      whole set printable, currently unlogged. Decide later whether
      the extractor (or a filtered subset) replaces the clone.
  [?] No listener-shape hardening exists: nothing wraps @serve in a graceful shutdown, a
      timeout or a rate limit; the guardrail refuses only the flag pair while
      `insecure_no_tls`-alone binds plaintext on the configured `bind` (default
      `0.0.0.0:8443` — ./config.sdd), so Bearer tokens cross the network in cleartext with a
      warn line as the only ceremony, and no branch restricts the bind to loopback. Decide
      later whether the posture gains a TLS-on-by-default rule, a loopback-only insecure mode,
      or stays warn-line documentation.

Done when:
  Every Scenario below maps to a green test in `server` (the `[ ]` Tasks or their successors),
    every `[?]` above is a recorded decision, `cargo test -p server`,
    `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo +nightly fmt --check` and
    `specdd lint` are green.

Scenario: Router surface and method defaults
  Given @create_router over any @AppState
  When `GET /healthz`, `GET` the base path, `GET` the instance path, `POST` any registered
    path, and unmatched paths — including trailing-slash variants — hit the @Router
  Then health answers `200` body `ok`, discovery answers `200` with the ./discovery.sdd body,
    a bare instance path without its fourth segment is unmatched, methods other than `GET` on a
    matched path answer `405` and unmatched paths the bare `404` — all axum 0.8.9 defaults, not
    @DiagError bodies
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Instance pipeline short-circuit order
  Given requests with {ns/name regex-failing, off-list kind, off-list item, valid shape without
    credentials, valid shape with denied SAR}
  When each reaches @instance_handler
  Then the legs end `400` `DIAG-003`, `404` `DIAG-004`, `404` `DIAG-005`, `401` `DIAG-006`,
    `403` `DIAG-001` in exactly that precedence — no identity read or cluster call before the
    auth leg, none before the SAR leg
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Dot runs in path params
  Given `{name}` values `..` and `a..b`, `{ns}` values `.foo` and `foo..bar`, `{kind}` and
    `{item}` values `..`
  When each pipeline runs its checks
  Then `..` `.foo` die at `400` `DIAG-003`; `a..b` and `foo..bar` pass the regex and, if
    authenticated and gated, hit the existence/collect lanes unchanged; `..` in kind or item dies
    at `404` `DIAG-004`/`DIAG-005` before the regex ever sees a dot
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Generic tier skips the existence gate
  Given a shape-valid, authenticated request for `clusterinfo`, or for `packages` with the
    enable flag set, or for `vynilconfig`, where the referenced `{ns}`/`{name}` pair is not an
    existing instance
  When it dispatches
  Then existence is never checked and the arm answers `200` with its collector's payload
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Existence failures answer not-found
  Given a gated item, an allowed SAR, and existence gets that yield the object, absence, an
    RBAC denial and an unreachable cluster
  When each runs
  Then the present instance dispatches as its item arm, and the three failure shapes all answer
    the same `404` `DIAG-002` — no log, no `500`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Nine arms and the X-Diag-Redactions matrix
  Given authenticated allowed requests for all nine items, collectors answering successfully
    with a @ScrubStats of `distinct=2`, `occurrences=7` where applicable
  When each dispatches
  Then `clusterinfo`/`packages`/`popularitycontest` answer `200` `application/json` with no
    scrub header, `children` `200` `application/json` and `state`/`vynilconfig` `200`
    `application/yaml` with `X-Diag-Redactions: distinct=2;occurrences=7`, `agentlog`/`childlogs`
    /`operatorlog` `200` `text/plain; charset=utf-8` with the same header
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Trust/insecure startup matrix
  Given @Config pairs {trust+insecure, trust+TLS material, insecure-only, plain TLS pair}
  When @run_server starts each with a bind address that parses
  Then insecure+trust returns the `500` `DIAG-500` payload containing
    `DIAG-CONFIG: --trust-request-header requires TLS` and serves nothing, trust+TLS loads CA
    and serves mTLS with the `MANDATORY` info line, insecure-only binds plain HTTP after the
    warn line, TLS-pair serves `from_pem_file` TLS after the `(server-side TLS)` info line —
    trust+insecure refuses before any bind or listener
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: CA load and mTLS builder failure legs
  Given an @config.requestheader_ca override file, then an override-unset ConfigMap get that
    fails, then one whose key is absent, and a key file with no PEM key
  When @load_requestheader_ca and @build_mtls_config run on each
  Then the override reads verbatim, a bad path yields the payload `requestheader CA file: …`, a
    get failure yields @DiagError::KubeError, the missing key yields the
    `requestheader-client-ca-file absent de …` @DiagError::InternalError, and the keyless file
    yields `mTLS config: no private key in key file` — every text `500` `DIAG-500` rendered to a
    log, never to a socket
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: TLS material half pair and bind ordering before the guardrail
  Given @Config with @Some cert @None key while insecure is `false`, and one with garbage bind
    and trust+insecure together
  When @run_server runs each
  Then the first yields `TLS certificates not provided for HTTPS server`, the second yields
    `Invalid bind address: …` — the bind parse error masks the refused-pair `DIAG-CONFIG:` text
    on the ./main.rs error line
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  @INSTANCE_PATH verbatim: `/apis/admin.vynil.solidite.fr/v1/namespaces/{ns}/{kind}/{name}/{item}`;
    full instance URL shape:
    `/apis/admin.vynil.solidite.fr/v1/namespaces/tenant-a/tenantinstances/web/childlogs`
  Scrub header literal: `X-Diag-Redactions: distinct=3;occurrences=14`; guardrail payload:
    `DIAG-CONFIG: --trust-request-header requires TLS (mandatory mTLS). Refusing to start in an impersonable configuration.`
  Guardrail rendered @Display: `DIAG-500: Internal server error - DIAG-CONFIG: --trust-request-header requires TLS (mandatory mTLS). Refusing to start in an impersonable configuration.`
  Insecure warn: `Starting HTTP server (no TLS) on 0.0.0.0:8443 — Bearer/TokenReview auth only`
